  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.read_source.fn` has one obligation. Criterion code must use `ValidationContext.read_source` for the read-source operation. The cited `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.ValidationContext.read_source` carries the behavior: resolve the outline item to its graph node, read the contents, and record the observation. That behavior is not reassessed here.\n\nThe requirement is implemented by `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs#impl[ValidationContext<'_, D>]/fn[read_source]`. It calls `source_node` and then `read`.\n\nThe marked test is `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[direct_source_reads_preserve_mapping_errors_and_record_only_successful_returns]`. It calls `ValidationContext::read_source` directly and checks these cases:\n- Mapping failures: an unknown file and an unknown selector both return an \"unsupported source item\" error. No dependency is recorded and no read happens.\n- Read failure: with `fail_read` set, the read error is propagated and no dependency is recorded.\n- Success: the returned content is correct, exactly one `Dependency::Node` with the content fingerprint is recorded, and the read targeted `source-node`.\n- Recorded observation: the finished record is current, and it becomes stale after the source text changes.\n\nThis exercises the public `read_source` API as the criterion-facing operation and asserts its outcomes. I found no unspecified or untested obligation. The test is marked with `{test}` for the subject, so there is no marking gap, and there are no `{fixme}` acknowledgments.",
